A||||7||Fiero_24||I need your help!!!||||9||
Z||000000||Fiero_24||08-17-2001||09:49 AM||||Today on the way to work the oil pressure light came on.  This was strange since I put a brand new sending unit in yesterday.  So I pulled over and checked the oil and it was full.  I started it and could hear ticking from the lifters (I am assuming they are dry), so I opened the oil fill plug and looked in witht he car running, no oil.  A little smoke came out of there and the dip stick hole too.  Could this just be the oil pump?  How hard are they to change?  Could the new sensor have shorted out the wiring to the pump?  I am lost here, and I need this motor to make it 1 more month until my Beefed up V6 is done.<P>Craig<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||9
Z||000001||Songman||08-17-2001||10:27 AM||||I can't really say anything about your problem but there is no wiring to the oil pump. It is mechanical and would not be affected by replacing the sending unit.<P>Since you hear the lifters ticking and can't see any oil flowing, I would say you have an internal problem if the oil shows full. The pump would be my first guess. And in my opinion, it is not worth changing an oil pump for one month's service.<P>Others may have other ideas about your problem. Good luck.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||grinthock||08-17-2001||10:41 AM||||I wouldn't drive it, youwill end up doing an AkursedX throwing a lifter or something.   <P>One comment though -- please refrain from using HELP!!!!! topics.  There is a subject line for a reason USE IT...  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiero_24||08-17-2001||11:00 AM||||The car is my daily driver, and I need to use it until the new motor is done.  If I had a second car, I would just park the Fiero.  What do you mean grinthock?  I need help on this asap before the car gets towed.  <P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||Joe Torma||08-17-2001||11:40 AM||||Put a mechanical oil pressure guage on it see what it says!  You need like 10psi oil pressure for each 1000rpm.<p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 08-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Philphine||08-17-2001||11:52 AM||||fiero 24, having something of the problem in the title dose at least two things.<P> as you go through the topic list and see oil pressure those who've had or are having that problem or just know something to help you might stop and read the thread more readily than one that just says help. i stopped on it but i can't help you. after a while at times when i'm short on time or something just seeing help in the title, even if it turned out that i knew something to help you, i might skip it.  <P>also in the future when you or the next person might want to go through search or the archives, when they put "oil pressure" in the subject search line, this thread and whatever help you get will have a better chance of coming up. <P>i admit i use kind of vauge subject titles at times but especially in the tech section i try to be as clear in the title as i can. it helps you and everyone else when you think about it. <P>no flames. just a tip.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>SERENITY NOW!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fiero_24||08-17-2001||12:39 PM||||No offense taken.  I was just in a hurry because I was mad and my car is in a Tow away zone.  I needed an answer fast.  I was not thinking to clearly.  I understand the help topics a little more.  I am usually good about posting better topics.  Sorry everyone!  I am going to try Oreif's idea.  Take 20w 50 and run it in there for a month until the new motor goes in.  If not then I will try the oil pump for a last resort.<P>Craig<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
Z||000007||maryjane||08-17-2001||01:55 PM||||It's a longshot but the oil pump screen may be clogged. I plugged mine up back in the spring, (did some work on the top of a badly gummed up cyl hd and knocked a bunch of gunk down into pan) oil light would come on after about two minutes. I drained the oil and poured in some solvent, shook the car on the springs, and let it sit for a couple of hrs, then drained and repeated it several times.  It made my 4cyl last a month and 1/2 till I could get a rebuilt put in. ||||reg||1
